        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-13 09:35:43.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20837 libcfs: move lustre_debug_vlen() out of line",
        "message": "LU-20837 libcfs: move lustre_debug_vlen() out of line\n\nOlder kernels built without CONFIG_OPTIMIZE_INLINING define\n\"inline\" as always_inline. lustre_debug_vlen() uses a va_list,\nwhich gcc cannot inline, so the build fails there, e.g. with\ngcc 8.5.0 on a 4.18 (el8) kernel:\n\n  lustre_debug.h:43:19: error: function 'lustre_debug_vlen'\n  can never be inlined because it uses variable argument lists\n\nMove the function to tracefile.c and leave a declaration in\nthe header.\n\nFixes: dbaef8ffa680 (\"LU-20837 libcfs: add tracepoints for Lustre debug messages\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I40d312cf43f48df275b13d360d0a8d0a69efcb1d\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
